# Copy to the repository root as CODEOWNERS and replace the handles.
#
# With require_code_owner_review on (tofu/github, off by default), a pull request touching an owned
# path needs an approving review from one of its owners. GitHub semantics: the LAST matching
# pattern wins, and a pattern with no owner removes ownership. General rows first, carve-outs last.
#
# A team as owner (@Test-Government/maintainers) must have write access to the repository and be
# visible; individual handles work without that.

# Everything: a maintainer reads every change.
*                   @OWNER1 @OWNER2

# The gate itself and what publishes: workflows, this file, release and chart publishing config.
# An author able to edit these unreviewed is not gated at all, whatever the ruleset says.
/.github/           @OWNER1
/CODEOWNERS         @OWNER1
